_licenses/              65+ SPDX license files with YAML metadata
_data/
  i18n/                Internationalization data (7 languages: en, fr, es, pt, zh, ko, ar)
    <lang>/
      ui.yml           Interface strings
      rules.yml        License rule labels
      licenses.yml     License summaries
  fields.yml           License metadata field definitions
  meta.yml             License rules taxonomy
  rules.yml            Shared permission/condition/limitation rules

_layouts/
  default.html         Base template with header, footer, language selector
  license.html         Individual license page template
_includes/             Reusable HTML partials (breadcrumbs, footer, sidebar, tooltips)

i18n/                  Translated prose pages (About, Community, No License, Non-Software)
assets/
  css/                 application.scss (compiled to CSS with dark mode support)
  js/
    app.js             Tooltip initialization, clipboard copy, GitHub API license suggestion
    i18n.js            Language selection and fallback logic
  img/                 Sprite sheet for home page triptych

spec/                  RSpec test suite
  *_spec.rb            License metadata validation, i18n consistency, HTML proofing
  spec_helper.rb       Config loader, license/SPDX/approval list fetchers

script/
  bootstrap            Install bundler and gems
  server               Run jekyll serve with incremental build
  cibuild              Build site and run full test suite (specs + HTMLProofer + Rubocop)
  check-approval       Print approved/potential licenses from OSI/FSF/OD
  generate-docs        (Present but not examined)

.github/workflows/
  deploy.yml           Build with polyglot + deploy to GitHub Pages on gh-pages push
  test.yml             Run tests on push and PR (⚠️ see note below)

Rakefile               Task orchestration (build → rspec → HTMLProofer → rubocop)
_config.yml            Jekyll config: collections, i18n langs, plugins, exclusions
Gemfile                Ruby dependencies
